  "details": "The default radius for bones in Dynamic Bones is 0, which causes a lot of issues trying to convert them when colliders get involved. Dynamic Bone Colliders can interact with bones that have a radius of 0, but PhysBone Colliders…don’t. \n\nA pretty hacky-but-easy fix would be \n\nif (DynBone[hair].radius = 0)\n{\nradius = 0.0000001 \n\n//just make it a value so tiny that it creates an output with negligible differences from DynBone radius 0\n}",
